{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-07T07:26:49.549Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"8a7db96ab021428362512547","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/6","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-07T07:26:49.549Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Corrected a tracker mistake introduced in the first task round: the rollout follow-up had been given the canonical gh:unbraind/pm-github#175 ownership tag even though pm-github-repeat-noop already owns that issue. This item tracks dependent caller adoption, not the original defect's ownership. Removed only this item's duplicate tag using pinned pm; retained all history and the canonical owner's tag. A regression prevents rollout follow-ups from taking the canonical issue owner's provenance."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-07T07:26:49.549Z"}],"before_hash":"98ff2c95fe1c78da9d616a1da600baa62576f2f52fb66c71d5aa567933a1fd33","after_hash":"c68330e456163a06419f47398499733f208730a7d8b79e4d2b7d98313af84754","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"c2b8f4c186baf32af6c9e97634028c4191e72a598447d6a538592901bd64ef4a"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-07T09:14:01.802Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"8a7db96ab021428362512547","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/7","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-07T09:14:01.802Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Clarified the watch matrix: the sync-only refusals in pm-beads and pm-memory require duplicate-owner repair, pm-ops requires configured completeness data/policy repair, and pm-jev requires source privacy remediation or a reviewed narrow allowlist. Both old and current releases refuse these cases, so a newer pin is recommended for diagnostics but is not their demonstrated cure. The other eighteen callers exhibit at least one release-fixed install, repeat-import or pagination class and need pin adoption; pm-brief, pm-rl and pm-changelog additionally need their documented caller repairs. This supersedes the earlier blanket statement that all twenty-two require a pin to resolve their observed refusal."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-07T09:14:01.802Z"}],"before_hash":"c68330e456163a06419f47398499733f208730a7d8b79e4d2b7d98313af84754","after_hash":"554fa8ce5b9224bc13c3e302de75ede4763d0f6501f1ac8fd869cd8398012ab6","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"ae3dfc04b67fb8c4eb00a9cb75bca4bfbdaa31805fea8ea4aef14642fa7f6f77"}
